  message: "DONE — PR #101. The baseline is honest again because the surface was DRAINED to it, not raised to meet it.\n\nMEASURED, NOT INFERRED. A worktree at dc17b03597 (the commit that last wrote the baseline) re-measures at exactly 1083, so the instrument is reproducible and the baseline was honest when written. Diffing the error SETS rather than the counts: 7 errors landed since, 3 were fixed by other work, netting the +4 (1087 on clean dev vs 1083 recorded). The item's filed figures (1090/seven, from a1d83f5e6d) were stale — seven PRs had landed since.\n\nTHE FORK, AND WHY (a) AND THE RE-BASELINE HALF OF (c) WERE BOTH DECLINED. update-baseline is documented for use after a PR REDUCES the surface or after an owner-approved config change; the ratchet is shrink-only by construction. Raising the ceiling to accept a breach is the move the design forbids, it ratifies the drift, and — the item's own words — it reproduces the condition. Same ruling shape as INV-zatug refusing to baseline cross_field|info at 9. So: option (b), fix the seven.\n\nTHE 7 ARE TWO TIGHT FAMILIES, NOT THE \"MIXED BAG SPREAD ACROSS UNRELATED MODULES\" THE ITEM FEARED.\n  - 5 bare generic annotations from recent work: make_route_symbol's extra_meta / meta (WI-zugob), the distinct_violations / _seen_flows pair (WI-kikis), _prune_grammars_to_used's list[dict]. Each given its real element type where one was recoverable rather than a blanket Any.\n  - 2 make_typed_stable_id arguments, and ONE IS A GENUINE DROPPED GUARD. go.py's interface-method site (WI-vibad) states in its own comment that it mints the typed stable_id \"exactly as the concrete-method site does\", then omits the conditional that BOTH concrete sites carry. A signature-less method would have formatted the None into the sha256 input and minted a real-but-wrong id where its siblings honestly emit None — the name-only key the typed id exists to avoid colliding on. It now guards as they do. In solidity.py the annotation was the defect, not the code: _extract_solidity_signature is declared Optional[str] but has one unconditional return and no failure path, so the return type is tightened and the call site's str-or-None disappears at its source.\n\nA STALE BASELINE CONCEALS PROGRESS TOO, AND THAT DIRECTION IS WORSE. The only delta remaining after the drain is index 21 -> 18: three errors fixed by unrelated work since 07-20 that the baseline never recorded. Because the ratchet compares per code, that recorded slack was LIVE HEADROOM — three new index errors could have landed with NO warning at all, where drift the other way at least printed one. Baseline now 1080, three below the number it had carried since the keystone landed.\n\nVERIFICATION. Per-code diff after the fix shows every code exactly at baseline and NONE above it, with index 21 -> 18 the sole delta — a precise confirmation that the drift and nothing else was fixed. mode=strict exits 0. Tests 8076 passed / 1 skipped / 4 xfailed / 0 errors, 100% coverage on changed sources. The go.py guard is covered by the existing WI-vibad positive control, which exercises a parameterised AND a zero-argument interface method; its else-branch is unreachable through valid Go, since normalize_signature_go returns None only for None or empty input and the extractor always returns at least an empty parameter list.\n\nSCOPE. This restores the instrument's honesty. It does NOT drain INV-zogud, whose surface is 1080 and whose flip is a separate multi-session grind."  # fec8
